   "start": 0,
   "end": 384
  },
  "info": "A demo for the Chord node. The chords lane has one Chord node with the seventeen chords typed into slots 00 to 10 (F# 13sus, Eb 9sus4, E 9sus4, E min9(11), G Major 7th, A 13sus, D Maj9, Db 7#9(no5), Db 7(#9#5), then F# min9, Db min9, A min9, B min9 twice over). Every pattern row has a single note, which only triggers; the Chd column says which slot plays, Oct the octave of the root (3 in the last eight bars) and Str the strum in ms.\n\nBars 0-7 move Bm9, E9sus4, A13sus, Dmaj9, Gmaj7, Db7#9, F#m9, Em9(11). Bars 8-15 do it again with an A min9 and Eb9sus4 on the way in and the Db7(#9#5). Bars 16-23 drift through F#m9, Dbm9, Am9 and Bm9, an octave lower. Bass comes in at bar 4, the drums at bar 8."
 },
